  "question": "An online retailer wants to maximize the profit by selling a gadget. The demand function is $p = 300 - 2x$, where $p$ is the price per gadget in rupees and $x$ is the number of gadgets sold. The cost to produce $x$ gadgets is $C(x) = 100x + 2000$. For what value of $x$ is the profit maximized? Find the maximum profit.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Revenue $R=(300-2x)x=300x-2x^2$.<br /><br />Profit $P=R-C=300x-2x^2-100x-2000=200x-2x^2-2000$.<br /><br />$P'(x)=200-4x$.<br /><br />Setting $P'(x)=0$ gives $x=50$.<br /><br />$P''(x)=-4<0$ so maximum.<br /><br />Maximum profit $=3000$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
